Zero-decimal currencies and deleted products in the admin panel. (1) MoneyInput keeps zero-decimal currencies (IDR after patches/shopper-core-idr-zero-decimal.patch) in whole units, so the 2-decimal price rule regex:/^\d{1,6}(\.\d{0,2})?$/ capped product, variant and shipping option prices at 999,999; zero-decimal currencies now accept up to 9 whole-unit digits. (2) Order items keep pointing at soft-deleted (or removed) products; the orders table cell, the order items list and the shipment detail no longer dereference a null product and fall back to the stored item name and the fallback image.

